IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc28-part24-s752.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, section 752 (PART XXIV, Dangerous Offenders and Long-term Offenders:
-- Interpretation, "In this Part"). Layer 1 of part ccc28. Imports the core (`ccc-core`) only: every section 2 answer it needs is an input.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in
-- parentheses after a defined term are not text to encode and are not quoted as such.
--
-- HOW EACH TERM IS ANSWERED. A function `s 752 ...` answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE    the facts bring the case within the term, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: here, "means" (every definition of this section is a "means" definition and closes its list);
--   NOTHING      not covered: the text is silent on the case, or a borrowed answer is itself not covered.
-- Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries a comment `FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words)` and the quoted words; every
-- branch that answers NOTHING carries `NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Functions in the section "Helpers" are not law: they carry an answer from their inputs (comments say `helper`).
--
-- WHAT THE PERSON STATES. The offence a person was convicted of is stated as a `s 752 offence`: the Code it is under, the provision (section
-- number as a decimal and subsection as the Code writes it, from the core), whether the conviction is for the offence itself or an attempt or
-- conspiracy, and two facts the former Code needs. A list in the text that names "section 85" without a subsection names the whole section: it
-- is entered with the subsection "", which matches any subsection of that section. A list that names "paragraph 81(1)(a)" is entered with the
-- subsection "(1)(a)", and the person must state the provision down to that paragraph to be matched.

§ `Helpers (not law): three-valued combination, lengths of time, a provision in a list`

-- helper: "both hold" over answers that may be NOTHING. A FALSE on either side is the answer; otherwise a NOTHING on either side is the answer.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 both hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN a   -- helper: carries the input's answer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN b    -- helper: carries the input's answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER b
                      WHEN JUST FALSE THEN b   -- helper: carries the input's answer
                      WHEN JUST TRUE THEN a    -- helper: carries the input's answer
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN a      -- helper: carries the input's answer

-- helper: "either holds" over answers that may be NOTHING. A TRUE on either side is the answer; otherwise a NOTHING on either side is the answer.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 either holds` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN a    -- helper: carries the input's answer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN b   -- helper: carries the input's answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER b
                      WHEN JUST TRUE THEN b    -- helper: carries the input's answer
                      WHEN JUST FALSE THEN a   -- helper: carries the input's answer
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN a      -- helper: carries the input's answer

-- helper: at least two of a list of answers hold. JUST TRUE when two are JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE when fewer than two could hold (the rest are JUST FALSE);
-- otherwise NOTHING (an answer that is NOTHING might make two).
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 at least two of the answers hold` MEANS
    IF count (filter (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- helper: carries the inputs' answers
    ELSE IF count (filter (GIVEN a YIELD NOT (a EQUALS JUST FALSE)) answers) AT LEAST 2
         THEN NOTHING   -- helper: carries the inputs' answers
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- helper: carries the inputs' answers

-- helper: the length of time in whole months (years are 12 months), and in days after the whole months; "less a day" takes one day off.
GIVEN t IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 752 the whole months in the length of time` MEANS (t's years TIMES 12) PLUS t's months

GIVEN t IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 752 the days in the length of time` MEANS t's days MINUS (IF t's `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- helper: a is at least b (months first, then days). "Two years less a day" is below "two years" and above "one year eleven months".
GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 752 the length of time is at least` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 752 the whole months in the length of time` a GREATER THAN `s 752 the whole months in the length of time` b THEN TRUE
        IF `s 752 the whole months in the length of time` a LESS THAN `s 752 the whole months in the length of time` b THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 752 the days in the length of time` a AT LEAST `s 752 the days in the length of time` b

-- helper: whether a stated provision is the entry of a list. An entry with the subsection "" is the whole section; otherwise the subsection must be the same.
GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`
      entry IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 752 the provision is the entry` MEANS
    p's section EQUALS entry's section AND (entry's subsection EQUALS "" OR p's subsection EQUALS entry's subsection)

GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`
      entries IS A LIST OF `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 752 the provision is in the list` MEANS
    any (GIVEN e YIELD `s 752 the provision is the entry` p e) entries

§ `What the person states about an offence`

-- The Code the offence is under. Paragraphs (c) and (c.1) of "designated offence" and paragraphs (b), (c) and (d) of "primary designated offence"
-- name provisions of the former Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, and the 1980-81-82-83 amending Act) or of this Act as
-- it read before a day the text does not name.
DECLARE `s 752 source of the offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`
    `s 752 an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970`
    `s 752 an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
    `s 752 an offence under this Act as it read before the day on which paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence comes into force`

-- "an attempt or conspiracy to commit an offence referred to in ..." (designated (d), primary designated (e)); "an offence or attempt to commit an
-- offence mentioned in" (serious personal injury offence (b)).
DECLARE `s 752 how the offender is implicated` IS ONE OF
    `s 752 convicted of the offence itself`
    `s 752 convicted of an attempt to commit the offence`
    `s 752 convicted of a conspiracy to commit the offence`

-- The date and the intent are read only where the text turns on them: the date for the former Code (paragraphs (b) and (d) of "primary
-- designated offence" and (c) of "designated offence" name provisions "as they read ... before" a date), the intent for former subsection 246(1).
DECLARE `s 752 offence` HAS
    `s 752 source` IS A `s 752 source of the offence`
    `s 752 provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `s 752 implication` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated`
    `s 752 date committed` IS A DATE
    `s 752 intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "serious personal injury offence" (a): the facts about the conduct, "in respect of another person".
DECLARE `s 752 conduct in the offence` HAS
    `s 752 in respect of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 752 the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 752 conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 752 conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `s 752 "court"`

-- Whether the court convicted an offender in relation to whom an application under this Part is made is a fact; whether the court is a superior
-- court of criminal jurisdiction is the answer of s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction", taken as an input.
-- src:16301 | court means the court by which an offender in relation to whom an application under this Part is made was convicted, or a superior court of criminal jurisdiction; (tribunal)
@ref s 752 "court" (src:16301)
GIVEN `the court is the court by which an offender in relation to whom an application under this Part is made was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 court` MEANS
    IF `the court is the court by which an offender in relation to whom an application under this Part is made was convicted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court means the court by which an offender in relation to whom an application under this Part is made was convicted, or a superior court of criminal jurisdiction"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" is itself not covered

