      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 212, "(4)")        -- (iv) subsection 212(4)

-- The provision is one of paragraphs (b), (c) or (c.1), whichever list belongs to the Code it is under. A former-Code offence is under paragraph (c)
-- only if the Code as it read before January 1, 1988 applies: the date the offence was committed is before that day.
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 752 designated offence (b), (c) or (c.1) the provision is listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence's `s 752 source`
    WHEN `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`
        THEN `s 752 the provision is in the list` (offence's `s 752 provision`) `s 752 designated offence (b) the listed provisions`
    WHEN `s 752 an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970`
        THEN     Day (offence's `s 752 date committed`) LESS THAN Day (Date 1 1 1988)
             AND `s 752 the provision is in the list` (offence's `s 752 provision`) `s 752 designated offence (c) the listed provisions`
    WHEN `s 752 an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
        THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 752 an offence under this Act as it read before the day on which paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence comes into force`
        THEN `s 752 the provision is in the list` (offence's `s 752 provision`) `s 752 designated offence (c.1) the listed provisions`

