       AND NOT (offence's `s 752 implication` EQUALS `s 752 convicted of a conspiracy to commit the offence`)
       AND `s 752 the provision is in the list` (offence's `s 752 provision`) `s 752 serious personal injury offence (b) the listed provisions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "serious personal injury offence means"

-- Paragraph (a): "an indictable offence, other than high treason, treason, first degree or second degree murder, for which the offender may be
-- sentenced to imprisonment for 10 years or more and involving any of the following in respect of another person, ...: (i) the use or attempted use
-- of violence against the other person, or (ii) conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of -- or conduct inflicting or likely to
-- inflict severe psychological damage on -- the other person".
-- "indictable offence" and "may be sentenced to imprisonment for 10 years or more" are read from the limb of the penalty provision the offender was
-- convicted under (the core's `Punishment`: its mode of proceeding and its maximum imprisonment), taken as an input (the offence's own section
-- states it). High treason is section 46(1) and treason is section 46(2); whether the offence is first or second degree murder is the answer of
-- Part VIII, taken as an input.
-- src:16384 | (a) an indictable offence, other than high treason, treason, first degree or second degree murder, for which the offender may be sentenced to imprisonment for 10 years or more and involving any of the following in respect of another person, including the offender’s intimate partner, a member of the intimate partner’s family and a member of the offender’s family:
-- src:16385 | (i) the use or attempted use of violence against the other person, or
-- src:16386 | (ii) conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of — or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on — the other person, or
@ref s 752 "serious personal injury offence" (a) (src:16384-16386)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
      `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limb of the penalty provision the offender was convicted under` IS A Punishment
      conduct IS A `s 752 conduct in the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 serious personal injury offence (a)` MEANS
    IF     `the offence is high treason or treason`
        OR `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than high treason, treason, first degree or second degree murder"
    ELSE `s 752 both hold` (`s 752 both hold` `the offence is an indictable offence` `the maximum is ten years or more`) `the conduct is within (i) or (ii)`
    WHERE
        `the offence is high treason or treason` MEANS
                offence's `s 752 source` EQUALS `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`
            AND offence's `s 752 provision`'s section EQUALS 46
            AND (offence's `s 752 provision`'s subsection EQUALS "(1)" OR offence's `s 752 provision`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
        `the offence is an indictable offence` MEANS
            IF `the limb of the penalty provision the offender was convicted under`'s `mode` EQUALS `by indictment`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence"
        `the maximum is ten years or more` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the limb of the penalty provision the offender was convicted under`'s `maximum imprisonment`
            WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` t THEN
                IF `s 752 the length of time is at least` t `ten years`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for which the offender may be sentenced to imprisonment for 10 years or more"
            WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limb states no imprisonment, so the maximum is not known from the section
        `the conduct is within (i) or (ii)` MEANS
            IF     conduct's `s 752 in respect of another person`
               AND (    conduct's `s 752 the use or attempted use of violence against the other person`
                     OR conduct's `s 752 conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person`
                     OR conduct's `s 752 conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "involving any of the following in respect of another person"

-- The whole definition. (a) is given the same facts; the answer of `s 752 serious personal injury offence (a)` and of (b) are combined: either one
-- brings the offence within the term; if neither does, and (a) is not covered, the answer is not covered.
-- This is the answer ccc22 asks for at s 606(4.1) (PLAN.md, seam 752).
-- src:16383 | serious personal injury offence means
@ref s 752 "serious personal injury offence" (src:16383)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
      `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limb of the penalty provision the offender was convicted under` IS A Punishment
      conduct IS A `s 752 conduct in the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 752 either holds`
                 (`s 752 serious personal injury offence (a)` offence `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` `the limb of the penalty provision the offender was convicted under` conduct)
                 (`s 752 serious personal injury offence (b)` offence)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "serious personal injury offence means"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) cannot be applied because the limb of the penalty provision states no imprisonment
